From 946bd12e9029ac1ea5dad9098392c97717919aa3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 366/488] soh: name the 24 address-named symbols defined in
 z_demo_6k.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 24 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Demo_6K/z_demo_6k.c.

  * func_80966E04 -> Demo6K_GatherLight
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the params 1 idle: plays NA_SE_EV_LIGHT_GATHER
    and the god-lightball loop until cue 6 reaches action 2

  * func_80966E98 -> Demo6K_ReleaseLight
    deduced, confidence HIGH: finishes the gather, spawns the params 2
    whiteout at frame 39 and kills itself at 64

  * func_80966F84 -> Demo6K_ExpandWhiteout
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the params 2 growth: pulses, grows the scale
    and fades the screen fill in, spawning EFF_DUST at frame 15

  * func_809670AC -> Demo6K_FadeWhiteout
    deduced, confidence HIGH: shrinks the whiteout away over 120 frames and
    kills the actor

  * func_8096712C -> Demo6K_PulseMedallionLight
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the params 3-8 idle: grows each sage light to
    0.1 and pulses it every other frame until cue 6 reaches action 2

  * func_80967244 -> Demo6K_SpawnSparkleBurst
    deduced, confidence HIGH: scatters EffectSsKiraKira in a sphere at the
    actor, tinted from sEnvColors

  * func_80967410 -> Demo6K_SageLightFollowCue
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the params 14-19 update: rides its own cue and
    bursts sparkles while that cue is on action 3

  * func_809674E0 -> Demo6K_FlyToTarget
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the params 9-10 update: pulses, then over
    frames 39-47 homes onto the fixed point -1611, 19, 1613 and dies

  * func_809676A4 -> Demo6K_SpawnSparkleTrail
    deduced, confidence HIGH: spawns eight EffectSsKiraKira scattered around
    the actor, scaled with it

  * func_8096784C -> Demo6K_RiseAndFade
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the params 11 update: drifts upward with a
    jitter, shrinking and trailing sparkles, dying at frame 24

  * func_80967A04 -> Demo6K_InitStreak
    deduced, confidence HIGH: seeds one of the sixteen falling streaks with
    its x, height, fall rate, color index and scale

  * func_80967AD0 -> Demo6K_UpdateStreaks
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the params 0 update: adds a streak per frame
    while cue 1 is on action 2 and respawns each as it reaches the floor

  * func_80967BF8 -> Demo6K_SpawnPlayerSparkles
    deduced, confidence HIGH: scatters 150 EffectSsKiraKira around the
    player

  * func_80967DBC -> Demo6K_GanonLightBlast
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the params 13 update: swells with
    NA_SE_EN_GANON_ATTACK_DEMO and NA_SE_EN_GANON_FIRE_DEMO, then bursts
    sparkles on the player and dies

  * func_80967F10 -> Demo6K_SpawnGanonBlast
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the params 12 update: spawns the params 13
    blast on its first frame and shrinks away over 60

  * func_80967FFC -> Demo6K_DrawLightBeams
    deduced, confidence GUESS: the params 1 draw: scrolls a tall texture
    through six per-sage color pairs; whether these read as beams or as a
    column of light is not settled by the code

  * func_80968298 -> Demo6K_DrawWhiteout
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the params 2 draw: fills the screen with a
    fading rectangle and draws the vertex-animated burst mesh over it

  * func_8096865C -> Demo6K_DrawFlash
    deduced, confidence HIGH: draws gEffFlash1DL or gEffFlash2DL billboarded
    and spinning, tinted from sEnvColors

  * func_809688C4 -> Demo6K_DrawStreaks
    deduced, confidence HIGH: draws the sixteen falling streaks at their
    recorded x and height, each in its own sEnvColors tint

  * func_80968B70 -> Demo6K_DrawGanonBlastSpawn
    deduced, confidence GUESS: the params 12 draw: a billboarded
    double-scrolling texture; named for the state it belongs to rather than
    for an identified effect

  * func_80968FB0 -> Demo6K_DrawGlow
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the params 13 draw: gGlowCircleSmallDL pulsed
    through a sixteen-step scale ramp

  * func_809691BC -> Demo6K_MoveAlongCue
    deduced, confidence HIGH: lerps the actor between a cue's start and end
    positions by the cue's frame span

  * D_8096930C -> sPulseScales
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the four-step 1.0 / 1.04 / 1.0 / 0.96 pulse
    applied to the whiteout scale

  * D_8096931C -> sStreakScales
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the four-step scale cycle applied to each
    falling streak

